     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Hi, what should the correct reaction be?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The error is due to the 'rel=type' field. if it was rel='type', it works, but with 'rel=type', in the code, it takes that string, tries to find if its equal to 'type', it isnt so returns null and then tries to do a sting operation on a null value. my solution so far is to filter null values and it completes that curl call with a 201 Created, which i'm not sure is what you're looking for?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Jon",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
