      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Hi, what should the correct reaction be?</p>\n\n<p>The error is due to the 'rel=type' field. if it was rel='type', it works, but with 'rel=type', in the code, it takes that string, tries to find if its equal to 'type', it isnt so returns null and then tries to do a sting operation on a null value. my solution so far is to filter null values and it completes that curl call with a 201 Created, which i'm not sure is what you're looking for?</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>Jon</p>\n\n<p> </p>",
     "created": "10/Nov/20 3:31 PM",
